  "curve": null,
  "notes": [
    "Player 0 acts first. Node names: open is player 0 at the root; after_check is player 1 after player 0 checked; facing_bet is player 1 after player 0 bet; facing_bet_after_check is player 0 after a check and a bet.",
    "The equilibrium is a one parameter family. The parameter a is player 0's bet frequency with J and may be anything in [0, 1/3]; every fact of kind affine is scale times a plus offset. A solver may land anywhere on the family, so a strategy check binds a from the solved J bet frequency first and compares the affine facts against that binding.",
    "Gate G1 checks the game value and the exploitability only (04 section 6). The strategy facts document the equilibrium family for reports and are not part of the pass rule.",
    "Exploitability is in chips, the ante being 1 chip, the unit the engine reports beside percent of pot. The pot at the root is 2 chips, so 0.001 chips is 0.05 percent of pot."
  ]
